<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pablo Morillo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1775–1837</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pablo Morillo was a Spanish general who led the large royalist expedition sent in 1815 to reconquer Venezuela and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a>. He besieged Cartagena and starved it into surrender in 1815, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a> in 1816 and carried out harsh reprisals against patriot leaders. In 1820 he signed an armistice with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a> and returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pablo-morillo.jpg" alt="Pablo Morillo" width="320" height="385" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Horace Vernet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pablo-morillo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
